{"id":"01KZWWAPY789MZ20QTVE8AZJPW","projectId":"01KZWVNGD4RM32PXWKEJXS69N6","type":"agent.completed","createdAt":"2026-08-13T06:18:08.711Z","nodeId":"schema","runId":"01KZWVNGD5XQY7GYMAMNAV585Q","message":"Derived the data model the approved Counter plan requires: exactly one table, public.counter, holding the single global counter row (id integer pinned to 1 by a check constraint, value integer not null default 0, updated_at timestamptz not null default now()), with a primary key on id, no secondary indexes, RLS enabled, and one policy — counter_select_public for select using (true). No write policy is declared, so the table is default-deny for insert/update/delete, which is what makes the approved plan's single audited mutation path (the increment_counter() security-definer function added by task T1) the only way the value can change. No ownership column and no auth.users reference: the PRD's stack line and out-of-scope list both exclude auth, and the approved plan's decision log makes the counter global. The scaffold's public.items table is deliberately absent from this schema plan — it is demo scaffolding the approved plan drops in a forward migration, not part of the data model this app requires. Every policy expression here references only the built-in literal true and objects this same plan creates; nothing depends on a function or table a later task introduces. This step was read-only analysis; the workspace was not modified and no commands were run, so no check is claimed as passing.","dedupeKey":"01KZWVNGD5XQY7GYMAMNAV585Q:attempt:01KZWW6JG76WSGATF0MCNBCQ5P:completed","data":{"modelId":"claude-opus","provider":"claude","durationMs":135425,"status":"completed","attemptId":"01KZWW6JG76WSGATF0MCNBCQ5P"}}
